9. Window Frames

A frame defines the subset of rows used inside a window.

Running total:

SUM(sales) OVER(ORDER BY orderdate ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)

Current + next 2:

SUM(sales) OVER(ORDER BY orderdate ROWS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND 2 FOLLOWING)

Previous 2 + current:

SUM(sales) OVER(ORDER BY orderdate ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)

Previous + current + next:

SUM(sales) OVER(ORDER BY orderdate ROWS BETWEEN 1 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)

Entire partition:

SUM(sales) OVER(ORDER BY orderdate ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING)

10. Frame Boundaries

Starting boundaries: UNBOUNDED PRECEDING | N PRECEDING | CURRENT ROW
Ending boundaries: CURRENT ROW | N FOLLOWING | UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING

11. Frame Shortcuts

ROWS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND 2 FOLLOWING  →  ROWS 2 FOLLOWING
ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW  →  ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING

12. ROWS vs RANGE

ROWS = physical row positions.
RANGE = logical/value-based range and considers peer rows with the same ordering value.

13. Quick Interview Mental Model

1. Which group? → PARTITION BY
2. In what order? → ORDER BY
3. Which rows participate? → ROWS/RANGE

